NVIDIA-proprietary components
-----------------------------
This image is not all Apache-2.0/BSD/MIT. It includes, under NVIDIA's own license terms and not under Apache-2.0:
  nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.7.1 and nvidia-cutlass-dsl-libs-{base,core,cu12,cu13} 4.7.1 (PyPI classifier
      "Other/Proprietary License"; https://docs.nvidia.com/cutlass/latest/media/docs/pythonDSL/license.html),
      required by both the vLLM fork (nvidia-cutlass-dsl[cu13]==4.7.1) and b12x (==4.7.1); the pinned base already
      ships nvidia-cutlass-dsl 4.6.2. It is a vendor runtime, like CUDA: nothing in this image modifies or compiles
      it, and b12x's and FlashInfer's CuTe-DSL kernels are generated by it at serve time on the GPU;
  the static CUDA runtime linked into the source-built libnccl.so.2 (NVIDIA CUDA EULA, redistributable);
  the CUDA runtime and toolkit components of the base image (NVIDIA CUDA EULA) and the nvidia-* CUDA library
      wheels torch depends on.
These are redistributed as the upstream vllm/vllm-openai base redistributes them. The OCI licenses label reads
"Apache-2.0 AND BSD-3-Clause AND MIT AND LicenseRef-NVIDIA-Proprietary".

